    "cellCounter": 7,
    "cells": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "code": "# Compute Pi with Archimedean Bounds\n\nArchimedes bounded pi between the perimeters of polygons drawn inside and outside a circle. This workbook uses the same idea without putting pi into the numerical recurrence: start with a unit-circle hexagon, repeatedly double its sides, and squeeze pi between a lower and an upper bound.\n\nThe first plot uses trigonometry only to illustrate the geometry. The bound calculation that follows uses square roots and the previous polygon's side length.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "code": "import numpy as np\n\n# Visualize the starting hexagon inside a unit circle.\ntheta = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, 200)\nangles = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, 6, endpoint=False)\nx_hex = np.r_[np.cos(angles), np.cos(angles[0])]\ny_hex = np.r_[np.sin(angles), np.sin(angles[0])]\n\ncircle = {\"x\": np.cos(theta), \"y\": np.sin(theta), \"mode\": \"lines\", \"name\": \"Unit circle\"}\nhexagon = {\"x\": x_hex, \"y\": y_hex, \"mode\": \"lines+markers\", \"name\": \"Inscribed hexagon\"}\nlayout = {\"title\": \"Archimedes starts with a hexagon\", \"xaxis\": {\"scaleanchor\": \"y\"}, \"yaxis\": {\"scaleanchor\": \"x\"}}\nmplot([circle, hexagon], layout=layout)",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "geometry",
        "lastOutput": "−2−1012−1−0.500.51Unit circleInscribed hexagonArchimedes starts with a hexagon",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<div class=\"plot-container js-plotly-plot\"><div class=\"plot-container plotly\"><div class=\"user-select-none svg-container\" style=\"position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%;\"><svg class=\"main-svg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"654\" height=\"250\" style=\"background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"><defs id=\"defs-0d7925\"><g class=\"clips\"><clipPath id=\"clip0d7925xyplot\" class=\"plotclip\"><rect width=\"439\" height=\"180\"></rect></clipPath><clipPath class=\"axesclip\" id=\"clip0d7925x\"><rect x=\"50\" y=\"0\" width=\"439\" height=\"250\"></rect></clipPath><clipPath class=\"axesclip\" id=\"clip0d7925y\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"30\" width=\"654\" height=\"180\"></rect></clipPath><clipPath class=\"axesclip\" id=\"clip0d7925xy\"><rect x=\"50\" y=\"30\" width=\"439\" height=\"180\"></rect></clipPath></g><g class=\"gradients\"></g><g class=\"patterns\"></g></defs><g class=\"bglayer\"><rect class=\"bg\" x=\"50\" y=\"30\" width=\"439\" height=\"180\" style=\"fill: rgb(22, 27, 34); fill-opacity: 1; stroke-width: 0;\"></rect></g><g class=\"draglayer cursor-crosshair\"><g class=\"xy\"><rect class=\"nsewdrag drag\" data-subplot=\"xy\" x=\"50\" y=\"30\" width=\"439\" height=\"180\" style=\"fill: transparent; stroke-width: 0; pointer-events: all;\"></rect><rect class=\"nwdrag drag cursor-nw-resize\" data-subplot=\"xy\" x=\"30\" y=\"10\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" style=\"fill: transparent; stroke-width: 0; pointer-events: all;\"></rect><rect class=\"nedrag drag cursor-ne-resize\" data-subplot=\"xy\" x=\"489\" y=\"10\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" style=\"fill: transparent; stroke-width: 0; pointer-events: all;\"></rect><rect class=\"swdrag drag cursor-sw-resize\" data-subplot=\"xy\" x=\"30\" y=\"210\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" style=\"fill: transparent; stroke-width: 0; pointer-events: all;\"></rect><rect class=\"sedrag drag cursor-se-resize\" data-subplot=\"xy\" x=\"489\" y=\"210\" width=\"20\"